WEBVTT

00:15.724 --> 00:17.934
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

00:18.017 --> 00:19.352
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

00:19.436 --> 00:22.272
EPISODE 5

00:22.981 --> 00:24.566
What department is your boyfriend in?

00:24.649 --> 00:26.735
-You promised to tell us.
-Well…

00:26.818 --> 00:29.821
Should I tell you an interesting story?

00:30.363 --> 00:31.489
You're curious, right?

00:31.990 --> 00:33.950
It's the story of my first delivery.

00:34.034 --> 00:35.744
You tell that story at every team dinner.

00:35.827 --> 00:37.912
Give it a rest, Twenty Questions.

00:39.289 --> 00:41.499
That's rich coming from you,
Screaming Devil!

00:41.583 --> 00:43.877
Please tell me, Professor.
I'm really curious.

00:43.960 --> 00:46.337
I was a first-year,
and it was the third week of September.

00:46.421 --> 00:48.047
-It was a Sunday, right?
-Yeah.

00:48.757 --> 00:51.926
All the professors had gone
to a conference in Busan.

00:53.094 --> 00:58.016
Then, a perfectly fine patient
suddenly went into labor.

00:58.099 --> 01:00.393
And I was the only one there
who could deliver the baby.

01:00.477 --> 01:04.355
When I called the professor,
I was told, "Prepare promptly!"

01:06.107 --> 01:07.358
and to deliver it well.

01:08.818 --> 01:11.738
Gosh, you could already see
the baby's head.

01:11.821 --> 01:13.281
Oh, no. Really?

01:13.364 --> 01:16.826
Hey, who was the one who called pediatrics
because the baby wasn't breathing?

01:16.910 --> 01:19.370
If I hadn't called them and performed NRP,

01:19.454 --> 01:20.663
you wouldn't be here.

01:20.747 --> 01:24.000
A baby less than 30 weeks old
and barely weighing 1 kg

01:24.084 --> 01:26.044
was trying to pop out.

01:26.127 --> 01:29.506
I heard you have to be careful
with their heads if they're too premature.

01:29.589 --> 01:31.716
-Did you perform an episiotomy?
-I did!

01:33.343 --> 01:35.762
Just as I was picking up
the episiotomy scissors…

01:36.763 --> 01:37.806
Um Jae-il!

01:38.973 --> 01:41.309
"CHEER UP" by TWICE!

01:43.061 --> 01:43.937
Correct.

01:45.438 --> 01:47.774
I didn't hear anything.
How could he get it so quickly?

01:47.857 --> 01:48.691
Everyone,

01:49.609 --> 01:50.527
I'm a former idol.

01:55.448 --> 01:56.783
Okay, next question.

01:59.577 --> 02:01.204
Um Jae-il!

02:01.287 --> 02:05.500
"Eve, Psyche &amp; the Bluebeard's Wife"
by LE SSERAFIM.

02:08.294 --> 02:09.462
He really got it right!

02:10.630 --> 02:12.799
-He really got it.
-Next question, please!

02:12.882 --> 02:14.634
Gi-dong, just hear me out.

02:14.717 --> 02:15.802
No, listen.

02:15.885 --> 02:17.846
Why didn't you answer your phone?

02:17.929 --> 02:19.013
Me?

02:19.097 --> 02:22.058
I'm working, so of course
I can't answer the phone.

02:22.142 --> 02:23.893
But you don't even work.

02:24.602 --> 02:26.437
-She's drunk, isn't she?
-Let's talk tomorrow.

02:26.980 --> 02:27.856
You want to break up?

02:29.065 --> 02:31.276
Hey, fine. Let's break up.

02:31.359 --> 02:33.278
That's what I've been wanting to say.

02:33.361 --> 02:34.654
I think she just got dumped too.

02:34.737 --> 02:37.198
You wanted to break up first,
so don't call me--

02:37.282 --> 02:39.033
Hello?

02:39.576 --> 02:40.785
Hey.

02:42.871 --> 02:44.706
Pick up, Hong Gi-dong.

02:45.373 --> 02:48.293
If you don't pick up, we're done.

02:48.376 --> 02:50.837
Your call could not be connected.
After the tone, please…

02:58.052 --> 02:59.053
Dried pollack.

03:00.179 --> 03:01.639
Is the dried pollack out now?

03:08.730 --> 03:09.898
It really didn't work out.

03:14.903 --> 03:15.778
Excuse me.

03:17.447 --> 03:18.364
Excuse me, I'm…

03:19.157 --> 03:20.408
I'm sorry, but…

03:21.659 --> 03:23.286
Could we…

03:25.455 --> 03:27.790
If you don't mind, could we sit--

03:27.874 --> 03:29.042
No, you can't sit with me.

03:31.252 --> 03:33.129
I'm having a get-together
with my colleagues.

03:33.671 --> 03:35.048
And I already have someone I like.

03:37.133 --> 03:38.051
Good night then.

03:44.224 --> 03:45.183
No, I…

03:46.142 --> 03:47.352
That's not what I meant.

03:48.353 --> 03:49.938
That's our dried pollack.

03:52.357 --> 03:53.566
That's ours.

03:58.238 --> 04:00.448
Weren't you
in the Yulje OB-GYN get-together?

04:01.908 --> 04:03.034
That get-together

04:04.160 --> 04:05.453
just ended.

04:13.127 --> 04:14.003
Oh Yi-young.

04:30.687 --> 04:31.562
I'm sorry.

04:52.125 --> 04:55.336
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

05:30.538 --> 05:31.539
Joo-young!

05:32.498 --> 05:33.416
Hurry up!

05:34.959 --> 05:36.461
She's going to be the death of me!

05:46.471 --> 05:49.390
Why put on sunscreen
when you'll be stuck in the hospital?

05:50.141 --> 05:50.975
I know, right?

05:51.059 --> 05:53.352
Do you even remember
how you got home last night?

05:53.436 --> 05:55.354
Just how much alcohol did you drink?

05:55.438 --> 05:58.566
Joo-young, I think my body
has gotten weak lately.

05:58.649 --> 06:01.319
I only had a few glasses,
and I got tipsy right away.

06:01.402 --> 06:03.279
Did you make any mistakes while drinking?

06:03.362 --> 06:04.989
You said you were with your colleagues.

06:05.073 --> 06:08.034
Of course not. How old do you think I am?

06:17.251 --> 06:18.336
What's wrong?

06:18.419 --> 06:19.587
What's with that expression?

06:20.421 --> 06:21.339
Hey!

06:21.422 --> 06:22.757
Cheers!

06:26.135 --> 06:27.929
I heard our juniors gave us new nicknames.

06:28.012 --> 06:29.764
No. We didn't.

06:29.847 --> 06:32.475
Oh, come on.
We know you guys have names for us.

06:32.558 --> 06:33.434
What are they?

06:33.518 --> 06:34.852
There really aren't any.

06:35.520 --> 06:36.395
I swear.

06:38.940 --> 06:40.108
No.

06:40.191 --> 06:41.859
No. Nothing happened.

06:42.401 --> 06:43.611
Nothing happened at all.

06:43.694 --> 06:44.570
No.

06:44.654 --> 06:45.488
Are you sure?

06:47.031 --> 06:50.118
You didn't start blabbering
and blast people with harsh truths, right?

06:52.161 --> 06:53.037
What?

06:54.288 --> 06:55.164
What?

07:01.462 --> 07:03.673
It's okay. I'm just really curious.

07:07.176 --> 07:08.678
What were they again?

07:08.761 --> 07:09.887
Legends?

07:10.888 --> 07:12.765
Our heroes?

07:12.849 --> 07:14.433
Stop being so boring.

07:14.517 --> 07:16.185
We're not that old-fashioned.

07:16.269 --> 07:17.353
What are they?

07:24.360 --> 07:25.194
Don't.

07:25.820 --> 07:28.698
Don't, don't, don't.

07:28.781 --> 07:30.283
Twenty Questions.

07:31.576 --> 07:32.535
What's that?

07:32.618 --> 07:35.246
You suffocate us to death
with never-ending questions

07:35.329 --> 07:37.165
whenever you open your mouth.

07:38.958 --> 07:40.877
That's hilarious.

07:41.794 --> 07:44.213
Kids these days come up
with the best nicknames.

07:45.173 --> 07:46.257
The Screaming Devil.

07:49.218 --> 07:51.304
It means you're a devil
who screams all the time.

07:51.387 --> 07:52.388
Clever, right?

07:55.183 --> 07:56.142
That's interesting.

07:57.185 --> 07:58.186
That's very interesting.

08:00.229 --> 08:01.439
You're Malig--

08:02.607 --> 08:03.649
That hurts!

08:04.484 --> 08:08.237
Geez. You look so innocent,
but your slaps really hurt.

08:11.073 --> 08:13.993
-Should we order some dried pollack too?
-Sure! I'm down!

08:14.076 --> 08:15.244
Let's do it!

08:25.171 --> 08:26.631
You did do something.

08:26.714 --> 08:27.924
You messed up.

08:28.799 --> 08:31.636
I had a bad feeling when you said
you had a team dinner.

08:32.136 --> 08:33.804
What did I say about drinking?

08:33.888 --> 08:34.889
Answer me.

08:35.681 --> 08:36.766
You said to watch my mouth.

08:36.849 --> 08:39.060
Yes, exactly.
Did you watch your mouth or not?

08:40.853 --> 08:43.314
Geez. You're impossible.

08:44.815 --> 08:46.359
I don't know who said such nonsense

08:46.442 --> 08:48.736
about your sibling
being your best friend in life.

08:48.819 --> 08:50.613
I bet they were an only child.

08:50.696 --> 08:54.116
At least you can end friendships.
You can't even throw your sibling away.

08:55.952 --> 08:58.246
I think I'll be late anyway.
Should I just not go?

08:58.329 --> 08:59.413
Shut your trap.

09:04.752 --> 09:06.671
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

09:11.133 --> 09:11.968
Good morning.

09:12.051 --> 09:13.219
Jesus Christ!

09:14.762 --> 09:16.430
Did you get home safe?

09:17.431 --> 09:19.350
Yes, I did.

09:22.103 --> 09:23.479
Hello.

09:23.563 --> 09:24.397
Hello.

09:29.151 --> 09:31.487
It looked like you drank a lot last night.
Are you okay?

09:33.281 --> 09:34.699
Yes, I'm fine.

09:35.491 --> 09:38.661
Kids these days seem to know
how to have fun without feeling awkward.

09:38.744 --> 09:40.913
Even with professors around,
they speak their minds.

09:41.747 --> 09:42.748
Right, Professor?

09:42.832 --> 09:44.375
Weren't you shocked yesterday?

09:46.002 --> 09:47.086
That's why

09:47.670 --> 09:48.546
it was fun.

09:49.255 --> 09:51.048
That's what get-togethers are all about.

09:52.383 --> 09:54.510
-By the way, Yi-young.
-Yes?

09:55.803 --> 09:59.015
The data on the preeclampsia patient
seemed to be a bit lacking.

10:02.893 --> 10:05.438
How about compiling about 20 more cases?

10:06.439 --> 10:08.107
Sounds good. Right?

10:10.151 --> 10:11.027
Yes, ma'am.

10:14.697 --> 10:16.365
She's acting so nonchalant.

10:17.033 --> 10:18.576
I just can't figure her out.

10:19.577 --> 10:20.870
Isn't that even more annoying?

10:22.496 --> 10:24.081
No, I actually like it.

10:26.083 --> 10:27.001
Have a good day.

10:28.586 --> 10:30.004
How dare she?

10:30.087 --> 10:31.839
OB-GYN ULTRASOUND REGISTRATION INFORMATION

10:44.602 --> 10:47.396
Ma'am, just a moment. She'll be here soon.

10:47.480 --> 10:48.939
Is something wrong?

10:49.023 --> 10:51.442
No, everything will be okay.

10:52.902 --> 10:54.403
It'll be fine.

10:59.241 --> 11:00.868
What? What's going on?

11:00.951 --> 11:03.245
Doctor, she's 12 weeks pregnant.

11:03.329 --> 11:04.372
But I think I see

11:05.039 --> 11:07.541
an ovarian tumor on the ultrasound.

11:07.625 --> 11:08.459
What?

11:09.752 --> 11:12.838
Ma'am, I'm just going to
take a look at something.

11:13.422 --> 11:14.298
Okay.

11:16.592 --> 11:17.927
Is this what you're referring to?

11:18.511 --> 11:19.428
Yes, that.

11:19.970 --> 11:21.013
This

11:21.097 --> 11:22.014
stool?

11:23.140 --> 11:23.974
Excuse me?

11:25.101 --> 11:26.769
And this is…

11:29.397 --> 11:32.316
a rather sizeable piece of stool.

11:35.236 --> 11:36.404
I'm sorry.

11:38.447 --> 11:41.200
Ma'am, have you been struggling
to go to the bathroom lately?

11:41.283 --> 11:44.120
Yes, I've always had constipation issues.

11:44.203 --> 11:46.747
But recently, it's gotten worse.

11:46.831 --> 11:49.291
I was going to mention it
during my appointment later.

11:49.875 --> 11:52.795
I'll prescribe you some medication
that's safe to take during pregnancy.

11:52.878 --> 11:54.130
Thank you.

11:54.964 --> 11:57.091
I didn't know ultrasounds
were this detailed though.

11:58.509 --> 12:00.177
Yes, I'll see you later.

12:00.261 --> 12:01.262
Okay.

12:09.019 --> 12:11.730
ULTRASOUND ROOM 15

12:13.858 --> 12:16.694
Dr. Um, did you seriously
call me here during my busy day

12:16.777 --> 12:18.154
just to look at some stool?

12:18.737 --> 12:19.572
I'm sorry.

12:20.656 --> 12:23.909
It looked just like
an ovarian teratoma from textbooks.

12:23.993 --> 12:25.536
And you're saying I missed it?

12:25.619 --> 12:27.580
No, that's not what I meant.

12:27.663 --> 12:31.375
Then what? You're saying a tumor this big
suddenly appeared out of nowhere?

12:32.793 --> 12:33.919
Don't you think it's strange

12:34.003 --> 12:36.547
to believe you could see
a tumor in the first place?

12:38.090 --> 12:38.966
Right.

12:40.134 --> 12:41.135
I'm sorry.

12:42.887 --> 12:45.514
I doubted it as well,
but I just wanted to make sure--

12:45.598 --> 12:46.932
I have a lot of patients today.

12:47.016 --> 12:50.102
Do you know how much they'll complain
if the wait time increases?

12:50.186 --> 12:51.812
Doctor, I'll teach him right.

12:51.896 --> 12:53.772
I was supervising him,

12:54.356 --> 12:56.525
but I had to stop by
the delivery room for a minute.

12:56.609 --> 12:57.526
I'm sorry.

12:59.028 --> 13:01.363
Dr. Um, there's a patient
waiting inside. Go on in.

13:02.698 --> 13:03.532
Can he go?

13:04.992 --> 13:05.826
Go.

13:24.178 --> 13:25.513
Hello.

13:25.596 --> 13:27.056
-Hello.
-Hello.

13:27.139 --> 13:29.892
Mom, when can I meet my younger sibling?

13:29.975 --> 13:31.644
Just three more nights to go.

13:32.937 --> 13:34.688
Ma'am, take deep breaths.

13:34.772 --> 13:36.357
We're almost there.

13:36.941 --> 13:38.692
Deeper. Take deeper breaths.

13:41.362 --> 13:43.572
About Ms. Jin Gyeong-hye,
who has cervical cancer…

13:43.656 --> 13:45.991
We need to perform a hysterectomy
during the C-section,

13:46.075 --> 13:48.369
so I've scheduled
surgery for next Thursday.

13:48.452 --> 13:50.538
Please check
if Prof. Ryu Jae-hui is available.

13:50.621 --> 13:51.622
Yes, ma'am.

13:51.705 --> 13:53.541
And tell him we'll get the consent form.

13:53.624 --> 13:54.458
Yes, ma'am.

13:56.043 --> 13:58.921
By the way, Professor,
don't you have the triplet delivery today?

13:59.004 --> 14:02.132
Yeah, we're doing a C-section
since the first baby's in breech.

14:02.216 --> 14:05.219
The patient has low platelets,
so we're doing general anesthesia.

14:05.719 --> 14:07.596
I'm worried about excessive bleeding.

14:08.097 --> 14:10.641
Right, did Nam-kyung book
three incubators?

14:13.519 --> 14:14.353
Sorry.

14:18.023 --> 14:19.483
Don't you need to go?

14:19.567 --> 14:21.277
-Pardon?
-It's time for GYN rounds.

14:22.945 --> 14:24.822
Right. I should get going then.

14:46.427 --> 14:47.761
Oh, dear.

14:48.929 --> 14:50.139
It is a recurrence.

14:50.222 --> 14:53.100
Yes. According to the chart,
she was fine for three years.

14:53.183 --> 14:55.895
But her follow-up CA-125
came back around 123.

14:55.978 --> 14:58.689
And the APCT and chest CT
show signs of recurrence.

14:59.648 --> 15:01.066
I see.

15:03.068 --> 15:04.653
What should we do?

15:04.737 --> 15:05.905
Well…

15:09.617 --> 15:11.368
-I'll explain it to her.
-Okay.

15:13.120 --> 15:14.580
What's my schedule for today?

15:15.331 --> 15:16.957
You have a myoma surgery at 5:00 p.m.

15:17.041 --> 15:19.168
The patient is on aspirin
due to a history of stroke.

15:19.251 --> 15:20.669
I've arranged a neurology consult.

15:20.753 --> 15:22.880
I've requested a cardiology consult
for her arrhythmia

15:22.963 --> 15:24.590
and ordered an operative risk scan.

15:24.673 --> 15:26.383
You are perfect, Doctor…

15:26.467 --> 15:28.969
-Kim Sa-bi.
-Right, Dr. Kim Sa-bi.

15:29.053 --> 15:30.054
Sorry.

15:33.933 --> 15:35.351
But, Dr. Kim.

15:36.185 --> 15:39.438
There must be
about 50 fibroids in this surgery.

15:39.980 --> 15:40.940
Fifty?

15:41.523 --> 15:42.358
Yes.

15:43.108 --> 15:45.819
Then, it'll take
about three or four hours.

15:45.903 --> 15:47.821
Yeah, that's right.

15:49.198 --> 15:51.533
But to reduce
the chance of fibroid recurrence,

15:51.617 --> 15:55.162
it's best to remove
as many visible ones as possible.

15:56.872 --> 15:57.706
I see.

16:00.876 --> 16:03.379
People who like OB tend to find GYN a bit

16:04.463 --> 16:06.256
tedious, right?

16:08.676 --> 16:11.887
Right. We do the same thing for hours.

16:11.971 --> 16:13.055
There aren't many

16:13.722 --> 16:15.557
dramatic events either.

16:15.641 --> 16:19.436
Yes, it can be a bit boring
when compared to obstetrics.

16:19.520 --> 16:22.106
-What?
-Oh, that's not what I meant…

16:24.692 --> 16:26.360
"Boring"?

16:27.111 --> 16:28.112
But you know what?

16:29.613 --> 16:30.864
That's a good thing.

16:31.532 --> 16:32.366
Look.

16:33.117 --> 16:35.369
You've already adapted
and gotten used to it.

16:35.911 --> 16:37.413
You're doing an excellent job.

16:37.997 --> 16:39.790
Is that so?

16:39.873 --> 16:40.958
Absolutely.

16:42.292 --> 16:45.379
So, I'm counting on you
for the surgery later.

16:47.214 --> 16:48.340
Keep up the good work.

16:58.350 --> 16:59.184
Hey.

17:01.437 --> 17:02.396
What's on the menu?

17:03.647 --> 17:04.732
I'm coming right now.

17:06.567 --> 17:07.568
He's not here yet?

17:08.068 --> 17:09.111
He's on his way now.

17:09.194 --> 17:10.320
How old is he?

17:10.404 --> 17:12.156
No, I'll pass. Sorry.

17:14.491 --> 17:17.119
He's your brother's friend?
Then he must be a lawyer too.

17:18.996 --> 17:21.081
No, it's okay. I said I'll do it.

17:21.165 --> 17:22.750
Okay. Send me his number.

17:22.833 --> 17:23.751
Thanks.

17:25.377 --> 17:26.712
Going on another blind date?

17:27.212 --> 17:28.756
Mind your own business.

17:28.839 --> 17:30.883
Didn't you say you had one last month too?

17:30.966 --> 17:31.925
We broke up then.

17:32.593 --> 17:34.511
-And now?
-Now, we're totally done.

17:34.595 --> 17:36.889
-You'll totally get back together again.
-Not at all.

17:36.972 --> 17:38.223
This time, it's for real.

17:39.141 --> 17:40.392
You've dated for seven years?

17:40.476 --> 17:42.061
And broke up about 70 times.

17:42.144 --> 17:44.146
That's being a bit dramatic.

17:44.229 --> 17:45.397
I'd say about 50 times.

17:46.190 --> 17:48.400
Where's Jae-il? I'm hungry.

17:48.484 --> 17:51.070
I'm here! Here's your hot
and fresh tteokbokki!

17:54.073 --> 17:57.201
What great choices.
Great combinations. Who made the order?

17:57.284 --> 17:58.577
-You did, didn't you?
-Yes.

17:58.660 --> 18:01.246
Are you praising yourself?
These were already in combo sets.

18:01.330 --> 18:03.207
Ordering combo sets was still a good idea.

18:03.707 --> 18:06.418
All right. You can have them all, Sa-bi.

18:06.502 --> 18:07.920
-Awesome.
-Where's the chicken feet?

18:08.003 --> 18:08.837
Right.

18:09.505 --> 18:10.839
Here you go.

18:12.049 --> 18:14.301
Nam-kyung, you're going
to wear a hole into your phone!

18:14.802 --> 18:16.303
You can't reach your boyfriend?

18:16.804 --> 18:17.763
They're on a break.

18:17.846 --> 18:18.680
Permanently.

18:18.764 --> 18:20.682
-Permanently for this month only.
-Hey.

18:20.766 --> 18:23.310
I can never tell
if they're together or not.

18:23.393 --> 18:25.395
Whenever I ask,
she always says they broke up.

18:28.107 --> 18:29.191
This one's not spicy.

18:29.942 --> 18:31.276
One original and one mild.

18:31.360 --> 18:34.238
You ordered them.
You don't even know what you ordered.

18:34.321 --> 18:36.573
Why is she so aggressive?
Because they broke up?

18:36.657 --> 18:38.408
-They're on a break.
-Permanently.

18:38.492 --> 18:40.077
Permanently for this month only.

18:40.160 --> 18:41.120
Hey!

18:41.203 --> 18:42.788
Nam-kyung, your phone.

18:46.375 --> 18:47.417
What now, Mom?

18:48.669 --> 18:51.338
Why are you asking an OB-GYN
about Auntie's leg numbness?

18:51.421 --> 18:52.256
I don't know.

18:53.006 --> 18:55.384
I mean, how would I know that?

18:56.051 --> 18:58.220
Mom, I need to go into surgery. Bye.

19:00.347 --> 19:01.765
-Was that your mom?
-Yeah.

19:02.307 --> 19:04.351
She always calls when someone's unwell.

19:04.434 --> 19:06.603
She calls about my grandma's indigestion

19:06.687 --> 19:08.355
or my aunt's cough.

19:08.438 --> 19:09.439
As if I'd know.

19:10.315 --> 19:11.567
Don't take it out on us.

19:12.109 --> 19:14.570
She always asks,
"Have you eaten? Are you sleeping well?"

19:14.653 --> 19:16.446
"Why can't you sleep?
Are you cold or hot?"

19:16.530 --> 19:17.739
Geez.

19:18.949 --> 19:20.200
Isn't your mom like that too?

19:20.993 --> 19:21.994
My mom doesn't call me.

19:22.828 --> 19:24.454
Is being indifferent hereditary?

19:25.080 --> 19:26.999
-You take after your mom, don't you?
-Yeah.

19:27.082 --> 19:28.333
My mom was beautiful.

19:30.002 --> 19:31.670
My mom doesn't seem to care much either.

19:31.753 --> 19:34.840
She's probably just busy.
I heard she's a professor.

19:34.923 --> 19:37.092
-How did you know?
-Prof. Jo mentioned it.

19:37.176 --> 19:38.760
She's at Bumyeong University Hospital.

19:38.844 --> 19:39.970
That's my dad.

19:40.053 --> 19:42.055
My mom recently moved
to Samho University Hospital.

19:42.139 --> 19:43.056
Are they both doctors?

19:43.891 --> 19:44.808
My brother too.

19:46.185 --> 19:47.436
A family of doctors.

19:56.320 --> 19:57.154
Yes?

19:59.448 --> 20:00.532
What is his problem?

20:04.077 --> 20:06.538
Okay. I'll be there.

20:12.711 --> 20:13.837
You're done eating?

20:18.258 --> 20:20.510
He failed today too.

20:22.387 --> 20:26.683
The intern keeps failing,
so the patients are upset.

20:26.767 --> 20:28.769
I'm upset too.

20:28.852 --> 20:31.521
Still, please don't be too hard on him.

20:31.605 --> 20:33.857
-Is it ABGA again?
-Yes.

20:34.524 --> 20:35.400
And…

20:37.194 --> 20:38.237
Tapping too.

20:38.320 --> 20:41.531
DRAINING EXCESS FLUID
FROM THE ABDOMINAL CAVITY WITH A NEEDLE

20:55.921 --> 20:59.049
I poked her right wrist several times,
so it'll hurt a bit.

21:01.260 --> 21:02.135
Damn it.

21:03.428 --> 21:04.596
I'm sorry.

21:16.316 --> 21:18.151
She'll make sure to do it
without any pain.

21:20.070 --> 21:21.154
Really?

21:22.281 --> 21:23.115
No.

21:23.865 --> 21:24.992
This will hurt a bit.

21:25.075 --> 21:26.952
It's normally a bit painful.

21:29.037 --> 21:31.123
Gosh. Okay.

21:40.257 --> 21:42.509
I couldn't see
the veins in her wrist at all.

21:42.592 --> 21:43.593
Be quiet.

21:48.640 --> 21:49.766
I've never done this before.

21:50.684 --> 21:53.854
I read that you should touch
the dorsalis pedis artery with one hand

21:53.937 --> 21:54.855
and--

21:55.731 --> 21:56.690
Seriously.

21:59.318 --> 22:01.194
I still have a lot of patients left.

22:01.278 --> 22:03.822
I'm already behind on my work,
so I need to be quick and go.

22:04.614 --> 22:05.615
I'm sorry.

22:08.869 --> 22:12.414
If there's something else to work on,
should I help with that?

22:12.497 --> 22:15.500
Forget it. Just stay still.
That's how you can help.

22:17.419 --> 22:19.254
Then maybe I could adjust the bed--

22:19.338 --> 22:21.298
Just shut up and get lost.

22:54.331 --> 22:55.665
Dr. Oh.

22:58.001 --> 22:58.835
I know.

22:59.669 --> 23:00.504
It's just that…

23:01.755 --> 23:03.006
I'm so busy.

23:04.633 --> 23:06.343
I was in a hurry and said it by accident.

23:06.426 --> 23:08.929
Even still, "get lost"?
In front of a patient, no less?

23:09.721 --> 23:10.722
I'm sorry.

23:12.140 --> 23:13.058
But…

23:13.809 --> 23:15.143
I did make a mistake,

23:15.685 --> 23:17.312
but he deserved to be scolded too.

23:17.395 --> 23:20.524
He said he couldn't do it.
The least he could've done was keep quiet.

23:20.607 --> 23:23.652
He was unable to do it,
so he was blabbering out of embarrassment.

23:23.735 --> 23:25.237
And I never said not to scold him.

23:25.320 --> 23:27.531
But if you're going to do it,
do it in private.

23:27.614 --> 23:30.242
I was too upset
at the time to think about that.

23:39.084 --> 23:42.671
Thanks to you, no one will want
to be treated by Dr. Tak.

23:42.754 --> 23:45.507
I bet the word's already spread
all over the GYN ward.

23:45.590 --> 23:47.342
He's just an intern, okay?

23:48.135 --> 23:50.178
He hasn't been here for even three months.

23:52.514 --> 23:53.348
I'm sorry.

23:53.849 --> 23:55.350
Can't you control your anger?

23:56.810 --> 23:58.520
Do you have to lash out to feel better?

23:58.603 --> 23:59.688
-Yes.
-Hey!

24:04.818 --> 24:07.070
I mean, no. I'll work on it, sir.

24:30.635 --> 24:31.887
You didn't press it.

24:33.513 --> 24:34.347
Right.

24:37.309 --> 24:38.727
You must be very tired.

24:42.189 --> 24:45.192
I raised my voice a bit earlier.

24:46.026 --> 24:47.360
I'm sorry. Are you upset?

24:48.945 --> 24:50.530
It's nothing to be upset about.

24:51.615 --> 24:53.617
And you don't need to apologize either.

24:55.660 --> 24:56.995
I deserved to be scolded.

24:58.455 --> 24:59.956
I apologized to the intern too.

25:00.540 --> 25:01.958
Good. Well done.

25:02.042 --> 25:05.629
Surprisingly, at times,
I notice you actually have common sense.

25:10.675 --> 25:12.552
It's already past midnight.

25:16.139 --> 25:17.641
SATURDAY, MAY 20

25:17.724 --> 25:18.975
It really is past midnight.

25:19.059 --> 25:20.727
What is it? Are you Snow White?

25:23.146 --> 25:24.231
Or was it Cinderella?

25:24.814 --> 25:27.776
It's not your first time coming home late,
so why are you so surprised?

25:27.859 --> 25:29.152
Today is my birthday.

25:31.947 --> 25:33.990
May 20. It sounds like "Oh Yi-young."

25:34.950 --> 25:36.284
I guess some people do

25:37.244 --> 25:39.079
actually name their kids that way.

25:40.664 --> 25:42.207
I mean, happy birthday.

25:44.501 --> 25:47.587
We live in the same house,
but you don't even know my birthday.

25:49.005 --> 25:52.008
I'm sorry. I'm not good
at remembering people's birthdays.

25:52.092 --> 25:53.969
But since it's yours,

25:54.052 --> 25:56.137
I'll buy you anything you want.
Just say the word.

25:58.515 --> 26:00.141
-Really?
-Yes.

26:03.103 --> 26:04.854
Then, instead of a gift,

26:06.189 --> 26:07.524
can you grant me one wish?

26:09.234 --> 26:11.403
Well, let me hear it first.

26:11.486 --> 26:12.779
Just do it, will you?

26:13.947 --> 26:15.031
Okay, I'll do it.

26:17.409 --> 26:18.743
Until we arrive home…

26:18.827 --> 26:22.080
So, until we reach the 14th floor,

26:22.956 --> 26:24.541
just say okay to everything I say.

26:33.300 --> 26:34.676
What are you doing? Get in.

26:45.645 --> 26:47.272
-Can you buy me dinner?
-Okay.

26:49.774 --> 26:50.650
Frozen pork belly?

26:51.985 --> 26:54.654
We already planned to eat
with our siblings next weekend.

26:54.738 --> 26:55.655
I'll pay for it then.

26:57.741 --> 26:58.575
Damn it.

27:04.706 --> 27:05.999
Can we watch a movie?

27:06.750 --> 27:07.584
Okay.

27:08.626 --> 27:11.546
I'll have Netflix and beer ready
on Friday night,

27:11.629 --> 27:12.964
so come out to the living room.

27:18.178 --> 27:19.054
Nine.

27:20.638 --> 27:21.473
Ten.

27:25.935 --> 27:26.936
Eleven.

27:30.857 --> 27:33.109
Can I like you?

28:12.315 --> 28:13.149
Okay.

28:27.997 --> 28:30.208
If you want things
to get awkward between us…

28:32.502 --> 28:33.503
then go ahead.

28:56.943 --> 28:59.612
Go a little bit later today.
We have something to do.

29:24.721 --> 29:25.972
Blow it out.

29:27.140 --> 29:28.641
Happy birthday!

29:28.725 --> 29:29.809
Happy birthday.

29:31.811 --> 29:33.438
Isn't it too early for a birthday party?

29:33.521 --> 29:35.356
Who knows what time
you two will come home?

29:35.440 --> 29:37.400
At least have some seaweed soup
on your birthday.

29:37.484 --> 29:39.861
Did you take a picture?
We should send it to your father.

29:39.944 --> 29:40.862
You're right.

29:47.535 --> 29:49.412
Hey, smile.

29:49.496 --> 29:51.206
How pretty!

29:53.416 --> 29:55.710
Time to score some points with Dad.

29:56.336 --> 29:59.005
I'll tell him I prepared
Yi-young's birthday meal in their stead.

29:59.088 --> 30:00.882
You didn't make this. Seung-won did.

30:00.965 --> 30:02.675
Yi-young, how did you know?

30:02.759 --> 30:04.677
Because it tastes good.
It's seasoned perfectly.

30:06.554 --> 30:08.473
Hi, did you see the photo?

30:10.934 --> 30:12.977
-He says happy birthday.
-Thanks.

30:13.061 --> 30:16.356
She's just like Mom,
so she loves a lot of meat in her soup.

30:17.357 --> 30:19.234
Seung-won did a terrific job.

30:19.317 --> 30:23.321
Are you doing well, sir?
I'm taking good care of your daughters.

30:24.572 --> 30:26.783
Yeah. Is work going well?

30:27.367 --> 30:32.038
Mr. Cheol-min isn't your friend anymore.
He's your boss. Learn well from him.

30:34.499 --> 30:36.668
Stop apologizing so much.

30:37.544 --> 30:40.296
Yi-young finally got her act together
thanks to your bankruptcy.

30:40.380 --> 30:43.466
Okay. We'll visit Busan sometime.

30:43.550 --> 30:44.634
Hold on.

30:44.717 --> 30:46.219
Hey. Damn it.

30:46.845 --> 30:47.679
Hey.

30:49.681 --> 30:50.557
Hi.

30:52.016 --> 30:52.851
What?

30:53.685 --> 30:54.519
I see.

30:55.353 --> 30:57.021
Yeah. Okay.

30:57.730 --> 30:58.731
Bye.

31:00.275 --> 31:01.109
Geez.

31:02.360 --> 31:03.528
Thank you for the meal.

31:04.320 --> 31:05.822
-Are you done already?
-Yeah.

31:10.159 --> 31:11.369
I'm heading out now.

31:11.452 --> 31:12.453
Be safe.

31:15.248 --> 31:17.292
Don't you have any gifts for me?

31:17.375 --> 31:18.710
Right, your gift.

31:18.793 --> 31:20.545
I didn't know what you'd like.

31:21.546 --> 31:23.673
-So I just wired you some money.
-That's not true.

31:23.756 --> 31:25.008
You know best what I like.

31:26.342 --> 31:27.510
Thank you, Seung-won.

31:30.471 --> 31:32.932
As a married couple,
that's our gift to you.

31:36.144 --> 31:39.772
OB-GYN
1ST-YEAR RESIDENT LOUNGE

31:40.440 --> 31:42.108
Hey, Yi-young. Happy birthday.

31:42.191 --> 31:44.027
Happy birthday.
The messenger app reminded me.

31:44.110 --> 31:45.778
You should've told us. Happy birthday.

31:51.701 --> 31:53.077
UM JAE-IL
HAS SENT YOU A GIFT

31:55.163 --> 31:58.249
Hey, I didn't have time to buy a gift.
Let's have a proper party next time.

32:01.002 --> 32:02.295
PYO NAM-KYUNG
HAS SENT YOU A GIFT

32:02.378 --> 32:03.296
Happy birthday.

32:03.379 --> 32:05.006
That's the most popular scent.

32:05.632 --> 32:06.799
KIM SA-BI
HAS SENT YOU A GIFT

32:06.883 --> 32:08.217
Happy birthday, Yi-young.

32:08.760 --> 32:10.803
I don't really know yet what you like.

32:10.887 --> 32:11.804
Happy birthday.

32:15.975 --> 32:17.977
They're so in sync at times like this.

32:20.647 --> 32:22.357
Right? It is, isn't it?

32:27.028 --> 32:27.946
Well…

32:28.029 --> 32:29.197
It's a girl, isn't it?

32:29.280 --> 32:32.533
Both my pregnancy dream
and the shape of my belly say it's a girl.

32:32.617 --> 32:35.453
The legs are crossed,
so it's a bit unclear.

32:36.579 --> 32:37.622
But it looks like a boy.

32:37.705 --> 32:40.541
No way. That can't be right.

32:40.625 --> 32:41.501
Are you sure?

32:42.460 --> 32:43.336
Yes.

32:44.212 --> 32:45.213
Doctor.

32:45.296 --> 32:48.007
I'm going through all this at 44

32:48.091 --> 32:50.593
just to have a daughter.

32:50.677 --> 32:51.928
Please check again.

32:54.514 --> 32:57.266
It's definitely a boy.
I'm very good at identifying the gender.

32:57.850 --> 32:59.268
Are you sure you weren't mistaken?

32:59.352 --> 33:03.189
The way it kicks feels
completely different than theirs did.

33:08.569 --> 33:09.654
I'm certain though.

33:12.573 --> 33:15.451
Then, ma'am, let me check
one last time to be sure.

33:15.535 --> 33:16.786
-Okay.
-Okay.

33:17.787 --> 33:18.663
Doctor?

33:19.455 --> 33:20.415
Again?

33:20.999 --> 33:23.084
Yes, just to confirm.

33:33.052 --> 33:33.886
Ma'am.

33:34.429 --> 33:35.304
It is a boy.

33:35.888 --> 33:37.265
Right? I was right.

33:37.890 --> 33:39.767
Wait. Is it really not a girl?

33:39.851 --> 33:42.937
No. Just as he said, it's really a boy.

33:44.397 --> 33:46.232
Goodness. How will I handle four boys?

33:46.315 --> 33:49.027
What am I going to do?
For crying out loud.

33:49.569 --> 33:51.112
It might be tough raising them,

33:51.195 --> 33:54.365
but having many brothers
could be fun and nice.

33:54.449 --> 33:55.491
I agree.

33:55.575 --> 33:58.786
And being the youngest,
he'll probably be very cute like me.

33:58.870 --> 33:59.912
Forget it!

34:01.622 --> 34:03.958
Well, at least the baby is healthy.

34:04.584 --> 34:05.877
You did very well.

34:10.048 --> 34:12.884
She had such high expectations,
so I wanted to be sure.

34:13.384 --> 34:15.219
Yeah, you're good
at determining genders now.

34:15.303 --> 34:17.472
Yes, I've really got the hang of it now!

34:17.555 --> 34:18.389
I know.

34:19.015 --> 34:22.518
Hey, congratulations.
I hope I won't see you again today.

34:22.602 --> 34:23.644
I'll get going then.

34:23.728 --> 34:25.730
Okay. Thank you!

34:28.941 --> 34:30.318
Mom!

34:30.401 --> 34:32.904
Turn on the Wi-Fi!

34:32.987 --> 34:34.238
Hurry!

34:34.322 --> 34:36.657
They're streaming the game right now!

34:37.658 --> 34:41.204
Based on what we saw in the imaging,
the cancer fortunately hasn't spread much.

34:41.287 --> 34:43.414
-The surgery shouldn't take too long.
-Hurry!

34:43.498 --> 34:45.708
-Right now!
-Hold on.

34:45.792 --> 34:48.002
Once we get
the tissue analysis results after surgery,

34:48.086 --> 34:51.422
we'll tell you what type of cancer it is
and its exact stage.

34:51.506 --> 34:54.467
-Hurry!
-Just hold still for a minute.

34:54.550 --> 34:57.428
You'll need to walk often to prevent
intestinal adhesions post-surgery.

34:57.512 --> 34:59.847
-Mom!
-Blood clots can form easily in the legs,

34:59.931 --> 35:01.933
-so just wiggling your feet in bed…
-Come on!

35:02.016 --> 35:03.226
…would be very helpful.

35:03.309 --> 35:05.394
Fine!

35:09.774 --> 35:10.775
There you go, okay?

35:13.694 --> 35:14.821
Nice.

35:15.738 --> 35:16.614
Doctor.

35:17.573 --> 35:19.492
Of course,
the surgery itself is important.

35:20.076 --> 35:23.704
But I heard some people who undergo
general anesthesia never wake up and die.

35:23.788 --> 35:26.249
My uncle's friend's brother
said he saw it happen.

35:26.332 --> 35:27.792
Well…

35:27.875 --> 35:30.753
We can't say there is
absolutely no possibility of that.

35:31.337 --> 35:34.340
But that's why
we do so many tests before surgery.

35:35.049 --> 35:37.176
-And everything checked out fine.
-I see.

35:38.553 --> 35:40.763
Maybe it's because
my husband isn't in Korea

35:41.347 --> 35:42.557
so I'm feeling anxious,

35:43.516 --> 35:45.476
but I've been having bad dreams lately.

35:46.352 --> 35:48.020
My mind has been running wild.

35:48.646 --> 35:51.274
-I see.
-Do your patients all wake up

35:51.357 --> 35:52.733
after their surgeries?

35:52.817 --> 35:56.112
Yes, we usually call out their names
when the surgery is over.

35:56.195 --> 35:58.489
And they all wake up just fine.

35:58.573 --> 35:59.574
Really?

36:00.324 --> 36:02.785
Then please call out my name loudly.

36:02.869 --> 36:04.787
"Na Se-jin!"

36:04.871 --> 36:05.788
Like this.

36:08.249 --> 36:11.252
If I still don't wake up,
please say, "Ko Min-jun."

36:12.336 --> 36:13.462
-Okay.
-You have to.

36:13.546 --> 36:15.339
You have to say it loudly.

36:15.423 --> 36:16.591
I understand.

36:19.260 --> 36:20.261
Ko Min-jun.

36:21.053 --> 36:24.557
How many times do I need to tell you
that we're not the only ones here?

36:24.640 --> 36:25.892
Turn the sound off.

36:26.726 --> 36:27.602
Hey.

36:27.685 --> 36:29.395
Fine!

36:32.106 --> 36:34.108
I'm sorry for always troubling you.

36:34.192 --> 36:36.694
It's fine. Please don't apologize.

36:38.237 --> 36:40.531
We can't even be sick in peace
since we're moms.

36:41.073 --> 36:42.783
So please don't apologize for such things.

36:42.867 --> 36:44.202
Thank you.

36:46.245 --> 36:47.330
I'm sorry.

36:48.080 --> 36:49.540
He's still young and immature.

36:49.624 --> 36:51.042
We're the same age.

36:51.626 --> 36:52.877
We're both ten.

36:52.960 --> 36:54.795
My goodness, I see.

36:55.588 --> 36:58.424
Gosh, you seemed so mature

36:59.217 --> 37:00.718
that I thought you were older.

37:03.721 --> 37:04.889
Hello.

37:05.389 --> 37:07.433
-I've explained everything.
-Okay.

37:08.017 --> 37:09.852
I'll make sure surgery goes well.

37:09.936 --> 37:12.146
I'll see you later in the operating room.

37:13.731 --> 37:16.067
Hello, Ms. Ha Jong-im.
How are you feeling?

37:16.150 --> 37:17.443
So-so.

37:18.527 --> 37:20.613
Doctor, am I

37:21.239 --> 37:22.490
getting the chemotherapy?

37:22.573 --> 37:23.532
Well…

37:24.116 --> 37:27.328
Your white blood cell count
hasn't increased yet, so not right away.

37:28.496 --> 37:29.372
Is that so?

37:30.373 --> 37:32.792
Then, she has to stay
in the hospital longer?

37:33.584 --> 37:34.752
For how many days?

37:37.171 --> 37:39.924
First, we'll give you
some immune-boosting injections.

37:40.007 --> 37:42.093
Then we'll do another blood test tomorrow.

37:42.843 --> 37:43.719
Okay.

37:44.428 --> 37:46.013
You had four surgeries in ten years

37:46.097 --> 37:48.516
and multiple rounds of chemo
and radiation therapy,

37:48.599 --> 37:50.351
so it must have taken a toll on your body.

37:50.434 --> 37:54.438
Also, a lot happened
during your last round of treatments,

37:54.522 --> 37:56.274
so it's taking some time
for it to recover.

37:56.357 --> 37:58.693
We almost couldn't do
the chemo then, but we did.

37:59.402 --> 38:01.112
I'm sure it'll go well this time too.

38:01.195 --> 38:02.613
Don't worry.

38:04.031 --> 38:08.202
My surgery will go well,
and you'll get chemo too.

38:08.286 --> 38:10.454
Then we'll both
be discharged in good health.

38:10.997 --> 38:12.957
I usually have good feelings
about these things.

38:13.666 --> 38:15.751
I see. Thank you.

38:15.835 --> 38:16.794
All right, then.

38:19.297 --> 38:21.215
-Excuse me, Doctor.
-Yes?

38:21.299 --> 38:23.050
Is Dr. Ki Eun-mi around by any chance?

38:23.134 --> 38:24.635
She went into surgery.

38:25.386 --> 38:26.554
I see.

38:28.806 --> 38:30.558
I'm sorry,

38:31.600 --> 38:33.394
but could I ask you for a favor?

38:38.649 --> 38:40.359
Of course Dr. Ki would do this.

38:44.071 --> 38:45.531
Why isn't your friend eating?

38:46.032 --> 38:48.701
He still needs his mom to feed him.

38:49.285 --> 38:50.786
As if he's still a kid.

38:51.996 --> 38:53.706
You are kids. You're ten.

38:53.789 --> 38:56.208
Some ten-year-olds are more mature.

39:02.423 --> 39:03.257
Who's that?

39:03.341 --> 39:05.885
My patient's daughter.
Her mom asked me to eat with her.

39:05.968 --> 39:07.219
I see.

39:19.774 --> 39:22.234
Geez, these damn ads.

39:22.318 --> 39:23.778
Just text him first.

39:24.695 --> 39:25.529
What?

39:25.613 --> 39:27.615
Text him first
if you're going to wait like this.

39:27.698 --> 39:28.908
No, I'm not.

39:28.991 --> 39:31.827
I'm not waiting for him.
What are you talking about?

39:34.830 --> 39:36.248
Do you want some water?

39:38.667 --> 39:39.585
Sure.

39:47.635 --> 39:49.261
1ST-YEAR OH YI-YOUNG

39:49.345 --> 39:52.431
You scared me!
I thought it was the delivery room.

39:53.265 --> 39:55.184
Sure, let's say that's what you thought.

40:00.147 --> 40:02.733
LEE
ATTENDING DOCTOR: KIM SA-BI

40:14.036 --> 40:15.287
Excuse me, I'm coming in.

40:19.250 --> 40:22.002
I'm here to get
Ms. Lee Ok-sun's consent for her surgery.

40:22.795 --> 40:24.630
Could you draw the curtain?

40:25.214 --> 40:26.048
Sure.

40:29.802 --> 40:32.096
You're scheduled
for uterine prolapse surgery tomorrow.

40:32.179 --> 40:34.890
Good grief. Why are you so loud?

40:35.474 --> 40:36.517
Mom, please.

40:36.600 --> 40:39.103
Everyone in this room
is going to find out.

40:39.186 --> 40:40.312
About what?

40:42.356 --> 40:44.859
You know, about my uterus.

40:44.942 --> 40:47.069
I told you it's nothing
to be embarrassed about.

40:47.153 --> 40:48.988
You don't know what you're talking about.

40:49.780 --> 40:52.658
They pretend like they don't care,
but deep down, they do.

40:54.160 --> 40:55.744
How utterly embarrassing.

40:55.828 --> 40:58.247
Mom, you've already
been admitted for surgery.

40:58.831 --> 41:00.416
We can't cancel it now.

41:00.499 --> 41:01.542
Right, Doctor?

41:02.209 --> 41:03.252
That's not exactly true.

41:05.629 --> 41:07.214
It would be best to do it though.

41:08.883 --> 41:10.926
How much longer am I even going to live?

41:11.010 --> 41:13.929
Why bother with such surgery at my age?

41:14.013 --> 41:15.848
Come on.
They said it's a simple procedure.

41:15.931 --> 41:18.392
Why would you want to live
in discomfort and pain?

41:18.476 --> 41:20.394
She's right. This isn't major surgery.

41:20.478 --> 41:23.063
We'll just pull up the part of the uterus
that has dropped--

41:23.147 --> 41:25.566
Goodness! Can you please be quiet?

41:25.649 --> 41:27.610
I said they can hear everything!

41:28.903 --> 41:31.405
We'll just check
that everything's secure post-surgery,

41:31.489 --> 41:32.948
and you'll be discharged right away.

41:33.032 --> 41:35.242
I'd rather not have it done though.

41:36.076 --> 41:39.288
It's not like I'm dying,
so why are you making such a fuss?

41:39.371 --> 41:40.456
Mom!

41:46.003 --> 41:48.297
LAPAROSCOPIC VAGINAL HYSTERECTOMY
CONSENT FORM

41:53.427 --> 41:54.845
About Ms. Lee Ok-sun…

42:01.727 --> 42:02.645
Prolapse. She's…

42:03.270 --> 42:05.231
-She's the patient from Busan.
-Yes.

42:05.314 --> 42:07.942
I explained everything
from the procedure to the consent form.

42:08.025 --> 42:09.944
Okay. Good job.

42:10.027 --> 42:12.154
But she doesn't want the surgery.

42:12.238 --> 42:13.072
What?

42:13.155 --> 42:14.740
She didn't sign the consent form.

42:14.823 --> 42:17.326
I think she was forced
by her daughter to come here.

42:17.409 --> 42:18.452
Really? But…

42:19.036 --> 42:21.413
She came all the way to Seoul
and had the tests.

42:21.497 --> 42:22.414
Right.

42:22.498 --> 42:24.583
Her WBC and CRP levels are normal,

42:24.667 --> 42:27.211
but she has vaginal discharge
and a severe foul odor.

42:27.294 --> 42:28.546
Then she needs the surgery.

42:29.380 --> 42:30.965
Why? Why won't she do it?

42:31.048 --> 42:33.008
She's ashamed about the illness

42:33.092 --> 42:35.177
and doesn't want others
to find out about it.

42:35.761 --> 42:37.596
Oh, dear.

42:39.139 --> 42:41.600
There is no such thing
as an embarrassing illness.

42:41.684 --> 42:42.518
Right?

42:46.564 --> 42:47.731
In that case…

42:49.066 --> 42:49.900
How about you,

42:51.193 --> 42:52.194
Sa-rang--

42:52.278 --> 42:53.112
It's Sa-bi!

42:54.196 --> 42:55.573
Right.

42:55.656 --> 42:57.950
How about our lovely Sa-bi--

42:58.033 --> 43:00.411
I'll ask if she'd like to sign
a voluntary discharge form.

43:00.494 --> 43:01.412
No.

43:04.081 --> 43:07.001
I think it'd be better
if she had the surgery.

43:07.084 --> 43:10.004
But we can't force her.

43:10.087 --> 43:11.213
Right.

43:11.297 --> 43:14.508
So please ask her one more time.

43:14.592 --> 43:15.426
Sorry?

43:16.010 --> 43:19.346
But I already explained it twice
in really thorough and detailed terms.

43:19.430 --> 43:20.848
I know, but…

43:21.682 --> 43:23.851
In Korea, people believe
in the rule of three.

43:26.312 --> 43:27.438
Rock, paper, scissors.

43:28.439 --> 43:29.356
High, middle, low.

43:31.317 --> 43:33.193
-Three Meals a Day.
-What?

43:35.446 --> 43:36.780
Gosh, Three Meals a Day.

43:36.864 --> 43:39.658
Just once more.
Let's ask her one more time.

43:40.909 --> 43:41.744
Okay.

43:43.579 --> 43:44.538
I'm counting on you.

43:46.332 --> 43:47.166
You can do it.

43:53.172 --> 43:55.633
-I can do it.
-Yeah. Third time's the charm.

43:55.716 --> 43:56.717
Good.

43:58.052 --> 43:58.886
We can do it.

43:59.637 --> 44:01.889
Yeah, the three of us.

44:09.438 --> 44:10.522
Doctor.

44:13.108 --> 44:14.276
Doctor?

44:17.321 --> 44:18.238
Doctor.

44:18.739 --> 44:22.868
Do you know when his mom
will be done with surgery?

44:22.951 --> 44:24.161
What's her name?

44:27.414 --> 44:28.749
What's your mom's name?

44:30.167 --> 44:31.335
Na Se-jin.

44:32.461 --> 44:33.629
It's Na Se-jin.

44:35.130 --> 44:36.256
Ms. Na Se-jin.

44:36.340 --> 44:37.424
Just a minute.

44:48.852 --> 44:50.854
Ms. Na, you're all done with surgery.

44:53.899 --> 44:55.776
-Let's take her to the recovery room.
-Okay.

44:55.859 --> 44:57.319
Submit her specimen on your way back

44:57.403 --> 44:59.988
and prescribe the medications
used during surgery.

45:00.072 --> 45:01.365
Yes, Doctor.

45:03.325 --> 45:04.410
Ms. Na.

45:07.121 --> 45:08.414
Ms. Na.

45:10.624 --> 45:12.459
Ma'am, don't you move! You'll fall!

45:12.543 --> 45:14.711
-Ma'am, please don't move!
-No!

45:14.795 --> 45:15.712
Ma'am!

45:15.796 --> 45:17.506
Ma'am, this is the operating room.

45:18.090 --> 45:20.384
Yes, you're awake. You're alive.

45:20.467 --> 45:23.011
This isn't the afterlife.
You're still in the real world.

45:23.095 --> 45:24.179
You're alive!

45:45.367 --> 45:48.036
I'm sorry. She's okay now.

45:48.120 --> 45:50.622
It's okay. This is nothing new.

45:51.832 --> 45:54.418
I was wondering why it was so quiet today.

45:56.086 --> 45:58.088
You're Oh Yi-young after all, right?

45:58.922 --> 46:00.090
Gosh, Oh Yi-young.

46:09.266 --> 46:11.727
-Yi-young! Can you do me a favor?
-No.

46:11.810 --> 46:14.021
-Can you just deliver this for me?
-Do it yourself.

46:14.104 --> 46:16.273
I need to go to the ER.
My transferred patient is here.

46:16.356 --> 46:19.526
-Just ask them to pick it up at the ER.
-Just leave this in Dr. Ku's office!

46:21.737 --> 46:25.240
She always pretends to be cold,
but still helps in the end.

46:26.200 --> 46:27.201
Right!

46:28.202 --> 46:34.208
OB-GYN
4TH-YEAR RESIDENT LOUNGE

46:34.291 --> 46:35.584
Doctor, it's Oh Yi-young.

46:36.335 --> 46:37.753
I brought the medical certificate.

48:23.900 --> 48:26.153
Do-won, did you check on Ms. Park Seol-a?

48:26.236 --> 48:27.070
Yes, ma'am.

48:29.239 --> 48:32.492
She said her blood pressure
was 140 over 90 at home.

48:32.576 --> 48:36.246
So we retook it,
and it came out normal at 118 over 78.

48:36.330 --> 48:38.957
I didn't suspect preeclampsia,
so I sent her home.

48:39.041 --> 48:39.958
Well done.

48:40.042 --> 48:42.377
Why hasn't Eun-mi updated me
on Ms. So A-jeong?

48:44.463 --> 48:45.672
One moment, please.

48:46.256 --> 48:47.382
We're using oxytocin.

48:47.466 --> 48:49.718
On the last pelvic exam,
the cervix was fingertip soft.

48:49.801 --> 48:51.803
Contractions are steady
at three-minute intervals.

48:51.887 --> 48:55.474
I'll tell Dr. Ki to notify you right away.

48:55.557 --> 48:56.391
I'm sorry.

48:56.475 --> 48:57.476
And what is Da-hye up to?

48:57.559 --> 49:00.520
None of the discharged patients
in the ward had their stitches removed.

49:01.271 --> 49:02.939
I'll check on it. I'm sorry.

49:03.982 --> 49:06.777
Professor Seo's patients
are taken care of. Why are mine not?

49:06.860 --> 49:08.612
What's wrong with you all?

49:08.695 --> 49:11.365
During morning rounds, Dr. Seo personally

49:12.282 --> 49:13.283
did them herself.

49:14.951 --> 49:15.786
She did?

49:16.703 --> 49:17.871
Geez.

49:17.954 --> 49:18.955
How diligent of her.

49:19.456 --> 49:21.750
Anyway, go check the ward.
It's a total mess.

49:21.833 --> 49:23.293
Yes, ma'am. I'm sorry.

49:23.377 --> 49:26.129
Right. My surgery at 4:00 p.m.

49:26.880 --> 49:28.173
I want you to be there.

49:28.799 --> 49:30.467
Don't only assist Jung-min.

49:30.550 --> 49:33.428
I want to operate with the chief too,
not just the first-years.

49:34.721 --> 49:35.972
I'll be there, Professor.

49:36.056 --> 49:37.140
That's a promise.

49:43.063 --> 49:45.899
Gosh, does she think
you have nothing better to do?

49:47.317 --> 49:49.111
Aren't you here to ask me for a favor too?

49:49.194 --> 49:51.988
Me? No, I came here to compliment you.

49:52.072 --> 49:53.907
I saw the documents
you sent for the paper.

49:53.990 --> 49:56.660
Research on mothers
who received progesterone treatment.

49:56.743 --> 49:57.577
I like that.

49:58.745 --> 49:59.579
Thank you.

50:00.122 --> 50:01.707
So I was thinking…

50:01.790 --> 50:05.377
You might as well compile the results too
since you have all the data.

50:06.503 --> 50:08.046
Would the workload be too much then?

50:10.507 --> 50:12.384
No, I'll do that too.

50:12.467 --> 50:15.637
Okay. I think that'd be more efficient.

50:16.221 --> 50:17.097
Right.

50:21.059 --> 50:23.478
-I need to go to the ward.
-Okay. Go ahead.

50:26.106 --> 50:26.940
Yes?

50:27.733 --> 50:28.567
Okay.

50:29.151 --> 50:30.652
I'll check and let you know.

50:37.325 --> 50:38.160
It's okay.

50:39.411 --> 50:41.830
Your cervical length
is maintaining well at 2 cm.

50:41.913 --> 50:42.998
Really?

50:43.707 --> 50:44.791
Thank goodness.

50:45.375 --> 50:47.502
My stomach hurt about an hour ago.

50:47.586 --> 50:49.421
Oh, dear. Is that so?

50:50.255 --> 50:52.340
Don't worry. Everything is fine.

50:53.425 --> 50:55.427
Does this mean I can return to the ward?

50:55.510 --> 50:56.344
Yes.

51:03.393 --> 51:06.521
By the way, did your stomach hurt a lot?

51:08.899 --> 51:11.485
It hurt about once or twice
during that hour.

51:12.110 --> 51:13.195
And

51:13.737 --> 51:15.614
it felt like my insides were sinking.

51:17.324 --> 51:20.786
I examined you thoroughly,
so I think you should be fine to go.

51:22.537 --> 51:25.165
But maybe we should check one last time.

51:25.749 --> 51:28.877
Why? Is something wrong? Is it bad?

51:28.960 --> 51:31.338
No. It's nothing like that.

51:33.799 --> 51:34.966
But it's just to check.

51:35.509 --> 51:36.968
It's better to be safe than sorry.

51:41.765 --> 51:44.518
I'll call her this time.

51:45.185 --> 51:47.687
Okay. Sure, go ahead.

51:52.317 --> 51:55.821
Ma'am, your cervical length is 2 cm.

51:55.904 --> 51:57.155
Right? It's 2 cm?

51:57.239 --> 51:59.199
That's what I got too.

51:59.282 --> 52:00.826
Does that mean I'm okay?

52:00.909 --> 52:02.828
Gosh, I was worried for nothing.

52:02.911 --> 52:04.621
At this stage of pregnancy,

52:04.704 --> 52:08.959
you can sometimes experience
false contractions that come and go.

52:09.501 --> 52:11.628
Don't worry too much and try to relax.

52:11.711 --> 52:13.463
Okay, thank you.

52:13.547 --> 52:14.506
Thank you, Doctor.

52:15.131 --> 52:16.007
You're welcome.

52:16.508 --> 52:18.510
Ma'am, you did very well.

52:19.135 --> 52:19.970
Thank you.

52:24.140 --> 52:25.809
I'm going to nap for just three minutes.

52:25.892 --> 52:26.726
Okay.

52:26.810 --> 52:29.896
By the way, just like I learned,
I didn't insert the probe too deeply

52:29.980 --> 52:32.858
and applied less pressure.
And that gave the exact cervical length.

52:33.441 --> 52:35.735
Yes, you were accurate.

52:36.361 --> 52:37.988
Yes, I was.

52:38.780 --> 52:40.031
Right, the consent form.

52:40.115 --> 52:42.075
I didn't get the consent form. Damn it!

52:42.617 --> 52:43.702
Have a good day!

52:46.288 --> 52:48.290
It's a real relief.

52:48.373 --> 52:51.793
There were no visible signs of spread,
and the surgery went well.

52:52.460 --> 52:53.378
Really?

52:53.461 --> 52:56.131
That's such good news.
You must be relieved.

52:57.507 --> 53:00.927
Of course, we'll have to look
at the biopsy results to know for sure.

53:01.011 --> 53:03.638
But based on the ovarian mass as of now,

53:03.722 --> 53:07.726
I think it might be related
to clear cell carcinoma.

53:07.809 --> 53:08.977
But this type of cancer

53:09.519 --> 53:12.647
is particularly prone
to developing embolisms.

53:12.731 --> 53:14.524
What's an embolism?

53:15.191 --> 53:17.152
It's when a blood clot blocks
a blood vessel.

53:17.235 --> 53:19.446
If it blocks a vessel
to the lungs or heart,

53:19.529 --> 53:20.739
it can be extremely dangerous.

53:20.822 --> 53:23.283
Embolisms are really dangerous.

53:23.366 --> 53:27.412
A lot of people who were on chemo like me
died because of that.

53:27.495 --> 53:29.289
It happens out of nowhere.

53:30.206 --> 53:31.041
Is that so?

53:31.124 --> 53:33.501
For now, make sure to exercise well.

53:33.585 --> 53:37.088
Let me know right away if you experience
any difficulty breathing.

53:37.172 --> 53:38.381
-Okay.
-Okay.

53:39.049 --> 53:41.051
And, Ms. Ha.

53:41.885 --> 53:44.095
Your immune levels
have improved significantly.

53:44.596 --> 53:45.680
We can proceed with chemo.

53:45.764 --> 53:47.599
Goodness. Am I getting chemo then?

53:48.099 --> 53:49.225
Really, Doctor?

53:49.309 --> 53:50.143
Yes.

53:50.810 --> 53:52.145
I'm so happy for you.

53:52.729 --> 53:55.231
I felt bad that
I was the only one who got surgery.

53:55.315 --> 53:57.567
I was worried
I wouldn't be able to get chemo,

53:57.651 --> 53:59.444
so I tossed and turned all night.

54:00.195 --> 54:02.280
We'll schedule it
after monitoring you tomorrow.

54:02.364 --> 54:04.449
For now, think of this as time to recharge

54:04.950 --> 54:05.909
and get plenty of rest.

54:06.576 --> 54:07.786
Thank you, Professor.

54:07.869 --> 54:09.329
My pleasure. Good day, then.

54:21.800 --> 54:23.802
Goodness. Who is this?

54:24.302 --> 54:25.136
Look who it is.

54:26.429 --> 54:28.098
Are you awake, my son?

54:39.067 --> 54:41.736
I booked a consultation room.

54:42.320 --> 54:43.571
It's empty right now.

54:43.655 --> 54:45.407
Would you like to
speak in private with me?

54:47.784 --> 54:50.578
Gosh, that's okay.
She'll have the surgery, so don't worry.

54:50.662 --> 54:51.579
Right, Mom?

54:52.288 --> 54:53.289
We agreed you would.

54:54.040 --> 54:56.001
You'll feel so much better
after the surgery.

54:56.084 --> 54:58.169
The recurrence rate is low on average,

54:58.253 --> 55:01.297
and according to research papers,
satisfaction rate is very high.

55:01.381 --> 55:02.382
Would you like to see?

55:02.465 --> 55:05.552
No, that's fine.
It's not like I'd understand.

55:06.219 --> 55:09.222
If you don't sign now,
today's surgery will be canceled.

55:10.098 --> 55:12.600
Let me ask one final time.

55:12.684 --> 55:14.436
Are you really not going to do it?

55:16.855 --> 55:18.773
My kids are barely making ends meet,

55:19.357 --> 55:21.317
and I'm already a burden to them.

55:21.401 --> 55:23.778
Mom, we can afford this much.

55:24.404 --> 55:25.822
Don't use us as your excuse.

55:25.905 --> 55:27.824
Well, you see…

55:29.284 --> 55:30.118
Goodness.

55:31.536 --> 55:35.290
Other old folks
don't get these issues and live just fine.

55:35.373 --> 55:37.542
I've lived a clean life,

55:38.334 --> 55:40.170
taken good care of myself,

55:41.379 --> 55:43.006
and lived modestly.

55:43.089 --> 55:46.342
As I've mentioned,
those things aren't related to this.

55:47.677 --> 55:50.305
The old ladies in my neighborhood
will beg to differ.

55:52.098 --> 55:53.850
Of course, they're all related.

55:57.520 --> 55:58.980
They have it all wrong.

56:00.273 --> 56:02.358
You shouldn't be friends with them.

56:02.442 --> 56:03.526
Ma'am.

56:06.279 --> 56:08.698
Do you know why you got this illness?

56:12.911 --> 56:14.370
Because you worked so hard in life.

56:19.084 --> 56:22.754
This is all because
you worked too hard in life.

56:25.590 --> 56:26.925
For the past 40 years,

56:27.467 --> 56:30.970
you've been tensing
your abdomen all day long

56:31.054 --> 56:33.306
while skinning eels
to pay for your son's wedding.

56:35.391 --> 56:36.226
And at night,

56:37.102 --> 56:39.187
you crouched in the kitchen
and washed dishes

56:39.270 --> 56:41.189
to pay for your daughter's wedding.

56:44.025 --> 56:45.443
That's why you're sick.

56:50.740 --> 56:53.701
Any parent would do as much.

56:54.452 --> 56:55.411
Exactly.

56:55.495 --> 56:58.039
So get the surgery now,
go back to your neighborhood,

56:58.123 --> 56:59.457
and brag about it to everyone.

56:59.541 --> 57:01.584
Tell them you got it
because you worked hard in life

57:01.668 --> 57:04.963
and that they should live
just as diligently.

57:05.880 --> 57:06.714
Goodness.

57:07.632 --> 57:10.176
I wouldn't have much
to brag about to do that.

57:14.973 --> 57:16.808
We'll make sure to be well-prepared.

57:16.891 --> 57:18.977
Okay. Thank you.

57:37.495 --> 57:39.080
Gosh, my neck.

57:39.789 --> 57:41.124
About Ms. Lee Ok-sun…

57:43.084 --> 57:45.128
I think she changed her mind
because of you.

57:45.211 --> 57:46.296
Really?

57:47.005 --> 57:48.840
Because of your story about the eels

57:49.549 --> 57:50.383
and dishwashing.

57:51.509 --> 57:54.971
When I heard it earlier,
I thought you were being too personal.

57:55.054 --> 57:56.181
What?

57:56.764 --> 57:59.601
But now that I think about it,
I think it was therapeutic.

58:01.144 --> 58:02.312
Are you saying I did well?

58:02.395 --> 58:04.564
Yes, sir.
I'll monitor her progress carefully.

58:04.647 --> 58:05.732
Good.

58:06.357 --> 58:09.110
I'm getting coffee. Do you…
No. Your shift's done, right?

58:09.194 --> 58:12.739
No, I heard there's an emergency cerclage,
so I'm going to observe it.

58:12.822 --> 58:14.866
-Right, Jung-min's surgery?
-Yes.

58:14.949 --> 58:18.620
I've never actually seen it in person.
But you're not going home yet?

58:18.703 --> 58:19.704
Me?

58:19.787 --> 58:22.582
I also have
a favorite type of surgery to do.

58:24.709 --> 58:25.877
Myomectomy.

58:28.213 --> 58:29.964
There are only five fibroids this time.

58:30.048 --> 58:31.841
The surgeries in Room 10
are running behind,

58:31.925 --> 58:33.718
so I'm starting in 30 minutes.

58:33.801 --> 58:35.053
I see.

58:35.136 --> 58:37.680
Wait. There's probably
no one available to help right now.

58:37.764 --> 58:40.433
Yeah, so I had to beg a fellow.

58:40.517 --> 58:41.392
It'll be us two.

58:42.143 --> 58:43.561
-Just the two of you?
-Yeah.

58:43.645 --> 58:46.147
But there's also the laparoscope, so…

58:48.024 --> 58:49.150
I guess three?

58:53.321 --> 58:54.405
Then…

58:55.573 --> 58:56.449
Maybe I could…

58:59.327 --> 59:00.161
It's okay.

59:01.246 --> 59:04.123
-But still…
-Don't worry about it. You don't have to.

59:04.207 --> 59:06.125
I can observe next time.

59:06.209 --> 59:07.043
Really?

59:08.044 --> 59:10.380
But really, you don't need to help.

59:12.131 --> 59:14.425
I mean, I feel bad.

59:20.848 --> 59:21.724
Then…

59:21.808 --> 59:22.892
In that case--

59:22.976 --> 59:24.435
I'll get going then. Good night.

59:26.229 --> 59:28.314
I see. You're leaving.

59:28.398 --> 59:29.524
Okay, goodbye.

59:31.025 --> 59:34.112
I'm sorry, Professor.
It's unlike them to miss things.

59:34.195 --> 59:37.031
But we had a lot to do in the ward
and delivery room today.

59:39.701 --> 59:41.452
No, I'll scold them properly today.

59:46.082 --> 59:47.417
Okay. I'm sorry.

59:53.548 --> 59:55.508
Knock, knock. Dr. Ku.

59:56.968 --> 59:58.344
I was just craving some coffee.

59:58.428 --> 01:00:01.139
I knew you would,
so I got you the largest size.

01:00:01.639 --> 01:00:02.473
Wait.

01:00:03.600 --> 01:00:07.061
-You want me to check another ultrasound?
-No. I'm good at that now.

01:00:08.187 --> 01:00:10.481
That's the best news I've heard all day.

01:00:11.065 --> 01:00:14.027
Sex, cervical length,
biometry, and amniotic fluid volume.

01:00:14.110 --> 01:00:15.445
I'm good at judging all of them.

01:00:16.237 --> 01:00:19.407
I'm probably the best at ultrasounds
among all the first-years.

01:00:20.491 --> 01:00:22.118
Aren't they all capable of that?

01:00:23.119 --> 01:00:24.162
Come on.

01:00:24.245 --> 01:00:26.497
That's not true. I really did well today.

01:00:26.581 --> 01:00:28.082
All right.

01:00:28.166 --> 01:00:29.083
I'm serious.

01:00:29.792 --> 01:00:32.795
Dr. Ki and Dr. Cha witnessed it too.
And they complimented me.

01:00:34.839 --> 01:00:36.674
-Eun-mi and Da-hye did?
-Yes.

01:00:37.550 --> 01:00:40.803
After I finished examining,
they came a few times to double-check.

01:00:40.887 --> 01:00:42.930
Every time they came to check
yesterday and today,

01:00:43.014 --> 01:00:44.641
I had everything right.

01:00:44.724 --> 01:00:46.059
I got straight As today.

01:00:47.727 --> 01:00:51.230
I'm so good that I think
I'm doing better than Nam-kyung.

01:00:54.067 --> 01:00:58.112
It's good that your diagnosis was correct,
but that's not the important thing.

01:00:59.072 --> 01:00:59.989
Sorry?

01:01:00.073 --> 01:01:01.741
You weren't confident in your judgment,

01:01:01.824 --> 01:01:04.619
so didn't you just ask
your seniors to cover for you?

01:01:06.829 --> 01:01:08.998
Eun-mi and Da-hye
are already busy as it is.

01:01:09.874 --> 01:01:12.085
But since you kept calling them
for ultrasounds,

01:01:12.168 --> 01:01:13.878
they must've been insanely busy and tired.

01:01:16.089 --> 01:01:17.298
That's being a nuisance.

01:01:17.840 --> 01:01:21.219
You may think you were right or did well,
but no one thinks that.

01:01:21.302 --> 01:01:23.429
You did what everyone can do.
What's great about that?

01:01:24.972 --> 01:01:26.015
Wasting others' time

01:01:26.099 --> 01:01:29.477
and getting them involved
because you won't take responsibility…

01:01:30.311 --> 01:01:31.479
That's incompetence.

01:01:33.815 --> 01:01:36.401
Think carefully
about what's right in the future.

01:01:47.370 --> 01:01:49.330
"If the placenta previa is severe

01:01:49.414 --> 01:01:51.332
or there's a large myoma
in front of the uterus,

01:01:51.416 --> 01:01:54.293
you should make
a J-shaped uterine incision around…"

01:01:54.377 --> 01:01:55.545
Yi-young, are you dead?

01:01:56.504 --> 01:01:58.589
Are you in a state of mental stupor?

01:01:59.424 --> 01:02:01.759
The professor told me to teach you two.

01:02:01.843 --> 01:02:04.846
Hey, you haven't seen this surgery either.
Are you listening?

01:02:05.638 --> 01:02:07.348
Are you two not going to study?

01:02:07.432 --> 01:02:09.308
They said we're going to
study this next week.

01:02:09.934 --> 01:02:11.686
Why worry about next week already?

01:02:12.311 --> 01:02:13.438
Just worry about tomorrow.

01:02:13.521 --> 01:02:15.022
-What's that?
-Cookies.

01:02:17.650 --> 01:02:19.736
A patient gave them to me as a thank you.

01:02:20.528 --> 01:02:22.405
Hey, you two. Come have some cookies.

01:02:23.322 --> 01:02:25.742
Hey, bread lover. You don't like cookies?

01:02:44.719 --> 01:02:46.471
Your boyfriend's taking a while this time.

01:02:46.554 --> 01:02:47.472
What do you mean?

01:02:47.555 --> 01:02:49.766
He hasn't contacted you
for a while this time.

01:02:49.849 --> 01:02:51.517
I'm not waiting for his call.

01:02:51.601 --> 01:02:53.644
I'm waiting for the delivery room to call.

01:02:53.728 --> 01:02:54.937
-Geez.
-Fine.

01:02:55.521 --> 01:02:57.648
Hey, is there only one box of cookies?

01:02:57.732 --> 01:02:59.358
Buy some with your own money.

01:03:01.027 --> 01:03:02.195
I don't have any money.

01:03:05.031 --> 01:03:08.910
The poorer I am, the hungrier I get.
How sad.

01:03:13.581 --> 01:03:15.625
But it's a peaceful night
for once, isn't it?

01:03:19.587 --> 01:03:22.673
I wish every day
could be this quiet and uneventful.

01:03:27.345 --> 01:03:30.973
OB-GYN, code blue.

01:03:31.057 --> 01:03:34.560
Ward 101, Room 1018. OB-GYN, code blue.

01:03:35.645 --> 01:03:39.357
OB-GYN, code blue.

01:03:39.440 --> 01:03:42.944
Ward 101, Room 1018. OB-GYN, code blue.

01:03:43.653 --> 01:03:45.988
-Connect the line, please.
-Epinephrine.

01:03:46.072 --> 01:03:47.031
Portable X-ray too.

01:03:47.114 --> 01:03:48.699
Run an ABGA.

01:03:55.122 --> 01:03:56.791
RESTRICTED ACCESS

01:04:06.926 --> 01:04:09.595
Her vitals were stable this afternoon.

01:04:10.596 --> 01:04:11.764
Then suddenly an hour ago,

01:04:12.473 --> 01:04:14.392
she complained of dyspnea and chest pain.

01:04:14.475 --> 01:04:17.061
Then her BP dropped, and her RR increased.

01:04:18.229 --> 01:04:21.440
Her vitals couldn't be stabilized,
so we performed CPR for 30 minutes.

01:04:21.524 --> 01:04:23.734
After her vitals returned,
we intubated her.

01:04:23.818 --> 01:04:25.862
But her BP wouldn't rise
even with vasopressors,

01:04:26.404 --> 01:04:28.281
so we transferred her to the ICU.

01:04:31.951 --> 01:04:33.369
Why all of a sudden?

01:04:34.579 --> 01:04:36.372
Based on the chest CT scan,

01:04:36.956 --> 01:04:38.791
it appears to be pulmonary embolism.

01:04:41.335 --> 01:04:42.253
Where's her family?

01:04:43.629 --> 01:04:44.881
She's waiting outside.

01:04:46.007 --> 01:04:47.800
-Let's bring her here.
-Yes, sir.

01:04:54.432 --> 01:04:55.766
Your mom

01:04:56.767 --> 01:04:57.894
is having

01:04:58.477 --> 01:05:00.646
some difficulty breathing right now.

01:05:00.730 --> 01:05:02.648
My mom's not dead.

01:05:04.734 --> 01:05:07.570
She has always been sick.

01:05:07.653 --> 01:05:10.489
I heard she's been sick since I was born.

01:05:13.284 --> 01:05:15.828
This is exactly like the last time.

01:05:17.330 --> 01:05:19.957
She was discharged then too.

01:05:24.879 --> 01:05:26.631
But the thing is, this time…

01:05:26.714 --> 01:05:27.632
Well…

01:05:42.688 --> 01:05:43.940
Is anyone coming for her?

01:05:44.440 --> 01:05:45.274
Yes, sir.

01:05:45.358 --> 01:05:47.360
There's a foundation
that sponsors the patient,

01:05:47.443 --> 01:05:49.362
and someone from there will be coming.

01:05:49.987 --> 01:05:53.741
It seems she's made
a lot of preparations in advance.

01:05:55.034 --> 01:05:55.910
I see.

01:05:58.788 --> 01:06:03.793
Then, until they arrive,
I want you to stay with the kid, Dr. Oh.

01:06:05.544 --> 01:06:07.463
-Me?
-Yes.

01:06:08.422 --> 01:06:11.092
Buy her something kids like,
such as ice cream.

01:06:13.511 --> 01:06:14.720
And

01:06:15.429 --> 01:06:16.847
explain things to her a bit.

01:06:16.931 --> 01:06:18.349
She's ten, so,

01:06:20.267 --> 01:06:21.936
she'll understand most things.

01:06:23.604 --> 01:06:24.438
Yes, sir.

01:06:25.022 --> 01:06:25.856
All right, then.

01:06:58.264 --> 01:07:00.224
I think your mom will go to heaven.

01:07:00.307 --> 01:07:01.434
No, she won't.

01:07:02.685 --> 01:07:04.812
You just don't know,

01:07:05.646 --> 01:07:10.276
but my mom always gets
really sick like this and gets discharged.

01:07:12.820 --> 01:07:14.321
It's for real this time.

01:07:14.905 --> 01:07:15.906
This time,

01:07:17.616 --> 01:07:19.201
she'll go to heaven.

01:07:20.119 --> 01:07:21.454
You don't have much time.

01:07:22.455 --> 01:07:25.332
So you need
to take a good look at her face.

01:07:26.625 --> 01:07:28.210
Is my mom really…

01:07:30.796 --> 01:07:32.048
going to die?

01:07:38.929 --> 01:07:39.805
Yeah.

01:07:54.987 --> 01:07:56.405
Then…

01:08:00.493 --> 01:08:02.161
what about me?

01:08:06.874 --> 01:08:08.542
I'm still

01:08:09.960 --> 01:08:10.961
just a kid.

01:08:11.545 --> 01:08:15.382
She's already found people
and places that will help you.

01:08:16.926 --> 01:08:18.010
They'll be here soon.

01:08:32.108 --> 01:08:35.152
Tomorrow at dawn or in the morning,
you might have to…

01:08:39.782 --> 01:08:41.492
say your final goodbyes.

01:08:43.035 --> 01:08:45.121
Don't say you won't do it
because you're scared.

01:08:45.621 --> 01:08:47.706
Tell her everything you want to say.

01:08:51.502 --> 01:08:52.419
And

01:08:53.295 --> 01:08:56.382
you'll have photos
to remember her face for a long time.

01:08:58.801 --> 01:09:01.387
But you'll forget
what she smelled like really fast.

01:09:02.388 --> 01:09:06.725
So make sure
you keep her clothes for a long time.

01:09:09.228 --> 01:09:10.312
Okay?

01:09:24.952 --> 01:09:27.746
There will be a funeral for three days
after she passes away.

01:09:27.830 --> 01:09:30.040
The person who's coming today
will help with that too.

01:09:30.124 --> 01:09:31.542
Just know that.

01:09:32.835 --> 01:09:33.752
Okay.

01:09:38.841 --> 01:09:40.342
"Don't cry from now on."

01:09:40.843 --> 01:09:43.012
"Be brave and good."

01:09:44.221 --> 01:09:46.223
"Eat well and study hard."

01:09:51.520 --> 01:09:52.438
That's what

01:09:54.023 --> 01:09:56.942
the people who attend
the funeral will say.

01:10:03.532 --> 01:10:05.201
Because they said the same to me.

01:10:15.377 --> 01:10:16.545
I was in middle school.

01:10:17.046 --> 01:10:19.798
That's when my mom
became an angel in heaven.

01:10:29.475 --> 01:10:30.893
But it's difficult to do.

01:10:37.900 --> 01:10:40.236
I wanted to be good and brave too.

01:10:43.072 --> 01:10:44.907
But I'd cry at random times.

01:10:46.575 --> 01:10:47.910
And I'd get so angry.

01:10:49.453 --> 01:10:51.747
I'd be so irritated
that I wouldn't want to eat.

01:10:55.584 --> 01:10:58.337
But that wasn't because I was a bad kid.

01:11:05.469 --> 01:11:06.720
When your mom dies,

01:11:07.638 --> 01:11:10.891
it leaves a hole this big in your heart.

01:11:14.645 --> 01:11:16.480
I still have mine. It's enormous.

01:11:20.109 --> 01:11:21.610
That's why,

01:11:22.736 --> 01:11:24.154
so don't hide and cry.

01:11:25.489 --> 01:11:27.449
Don't pretend to smile when you're sad.

01:11:30.286 --> 01:11:32.162
Just do whatever you feel like doing.

01:11:34.498 --> 01:11:35.332
Okay?

01:11:50.222 --> 01:11:51.390
Here's my phone number.

01:11:53.309 --> 01:11:56.603
If you ever have a hard time
or have any questions, call me.

01:11:57.438 --> 01:11:58.772
You can call me every day.

01:12:00.691 --> 01:12:01.525
Okay.

01:12:13.412 --> 01:12:14.288
Hye-min?

01:12:20.044 --> 01:12:21.295
Who are you?

01:12:22.212 --> 01:12:24.882
I'm from the foundation
that supported her mother.

01:12:25.758 --> 01:12:27.634
Hye-min and I have met often.

01:12:29.845 --> 01:12:30.679
I see.

01:12:30.763 --> 01:12:33.432
I heard her condition suddenly worsened.

01:12:34.058 --> 01:12:36.685
Yes, she was scheduled
for chemotherapy tomorrow.

01:12:37.561 --> 01:12:39.938
But she suddenly developed
multiple pulmonary embolisms.

01:12:47.029 --> 01:12:50.532
Then, what's going to happen to Hye-min?

01:12:51.950 --> 01:12:55.329
A relative her mother
mentioned before is on the way.

01:12:56.580 --> 01:12:59.416
And we'll continue to provide care too.

01:13:01.043 --> 01:13:01.877
I see.

01:13:02.419 --> 01:13:03.337
Thank you.

01:13:09.343 --> 01:13:11.011
I should get going then.

01:13:11.095 --> 01:13:11.929
Okay.

01:13:22.564 --> 01:13:23.482
Shall we sit down?

01:13:31.865 --> 01:13:33.117
You must be so scared.

01:13:34.201 --> 01:13:35.369
Are you feeling sick at all?

01:13:41.417 --> 01:13:42.668
You have a slight fever.

01:13:43.419 --> 01:13:44.461
Does your head hurt?

01:13:45.712 --> 01:13:48.298
I brought some medicine just in case.

01:13:52.636 --> 01:13:55.180
Should we get something to eat?

01:13:59.351 --> 01:14:00.644
Do you miss your mom?

01:14:07.443 --> 01:14:08.861
Let's go see her.

01:14:25.919 --> 01:14:27.588
Mom!

01:14:30.299 --> 01:14:32.050
Mom…

01:14:36.180 --> 01:14:37.764
Mom…

01:14:48.984 --> 01:14:51.778
Yi-young! Joo-young! Get up already!

01:14:53.113 --> 01:14:54.823
That shop was terrible.

01:14:54.907 --> 01:14:57.826
I bought cabbage from there last year,
and it ruined our kimchi.

01:14:58.368 --> 01:15:00.162
Really? You know a better place?

01:15:00.704 --> 01:15:03.040
Hey! Wash up and get ready to leave!

01:15:03.123 --> 01:15:05.042
Get up! Your food's getting cold!

01:15:05.125 --> 01:15:06.168
Seriously…

01:15:06.877 --> 01:15:09.671
Right, didn't you say
your second child was getting married?

01:15:10.172 --> 01:15:11.590
How old is she this year?

01:15:12.424 --> 01:15:14.927
That's right.
She's the same age as Yi-young.

01:15:15.886 --> 01:15:19.306
Gosh, when did our kids grow up so fast?

01:15:20.807 --> 01:15:22.726
I'm getting teary-eyed.

01:16:01.682 --> 01:16:02.516
Damn it.

01:17:37.110 --> 01:17:41.073
THANKS TO OUR SPECIAL GUEST,
YOO YEON-SEOK, OUR ETERNAL AHN JEONG-WON

01:17:41.573 --> 01:17:44.826
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

01:17:44.910 --> 01:17:47.371
I have the worst luck with colleagues.

01:17:47.454 --> 01:17:49.414
We're completely incompatible.

01:17:49.998 --> 01:17:52.834
Trying to talk to understand them
just makes things worse.

01:17:52.918 --> 01:17:53.877
You're so frustrating.

01:17:53.960 --> 01:17:55.671
I feel the same. You frustrate me too.

01:17:55.754 --> 01:17:56.755
I'm doing it right now.

01:17:56.838 --> 01:17:57.839
-Do it.
-Okay!

01:17:57.923 --> 01:17:59.633
They're always fighting these days.

01:17:59.716 --> 01:18:01.051
They just don't get along.

01:18:01.593 --> 01:18:02.761
Hey, first-years.

01:18:02.844 --> 01:18:03.970
I'm sorry, sir.

01:18:04.054 --> 01:18:06.723
-I thought you did it.
-I thought you would do it.

01:18:06.807 --> 01:18:08.642
"I read this in a textbook, so I know."

01:18:08.725 --> 01:18:10.477
I have no idea what to do.

01:18:11.061 --> 01:18:12.229
This is all your fault.

01:18:13.313 --> 01:18:15.023
Congratulations, Dr. Myeong.

01:18:15.107 --> 01:18:17.150
You were listed as a presenter
for the conference.

01:18:17.234 --> 01:18:18.902
Aren't you angry? Aren't you pissed?

01:18:18.985 --> 01:18:20.779
It really was my mistake.

01:18:20.862 --> 01:18:22.072
A mistake?

01:18:22.155 --> 01:18:24.866
Dr. Ku, I know you worked hard on this…

01:18:24.950 --> 01:18:26.159
Want to drink some soju?

01:18:26.243 --> 01:18:27.828
It's time to go home.

01:18:28.620 --> 01:18:29.705
You didn't go home again?

01:18:29.788 --> 01:18:31.289
Every night these days,

01:18:31.373 --> 01:18:33.250
you might not believe it, but…

01:18:33.333 --> 01:18:34.751
You look really tired.

01:18:35.335 --> 01:18:36.670
If it's okay with you,

01:18:37.212 --> 01:18:38.588
would you like me to take a look?

01:18:44.094 --> 01:18:46.096
Subtitle translation by: Sooji Kim
